title: As for Me and My House – Marriage, Family and the Home
description: Marriage, family and the home: God's order in the home, husbands and wives, divorce and remarriage, honour thy father and mother, and raising children in the nurture and admonition of the Lord, from the teachings on the family.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-family.html
highlight: child; wife; husband

# One deck for the doctrine "Marriage, family & the home" (76 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- As for Me and My House [title]
overline: Doctrine · Marriage, family & the home
heading: As for Me and My House
sub: Husbands, wives, children and honouring parents.
refs: Joshua 24:15; Ephesians 5:22-25; Ephesians 6:1-4; Deuteronomy 6:6-7; Psalms 127:3
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 13503
--- Every one his role
big: Colossians 3:18-21 | mark: Wives, submit yourselves; Husbands, love your wives; Children, obey your parents; Fathers, provoke not your children
p: Each person in the home has a Godly role and responsibility, as both servants and masters. Husband and wife. Parent and child.
p: Regardless of how well the others do at keeping up their responsibilities, you're commanded by God to keep up yours.
read: app:doctrine-family~13503 | Godly roles in the household

=== God's order in the home
# from 12446, 3851, 13605
--- The order of heads
kicker: God's order in the home
big: 1 Corinthians 11:3 | mark: the head of every man is Christ; and the head of the woman is the man; and the head of Christ is God
p: The “head” in this regard is not the physical body part but the ruler. The higher power each submits to. Submission isn't total helplessness. It is just the order of delegation of authority, God, lords, husband, wife, children, each with a role to play. Each requiring both sacrifice and responsibility.
p: The first half of 1 Corinthians 11 is about hair length: women are to have long hair, men short ([[1 Corinthians 11:14-15]]). If a woman thinks she should wear a covering, it's not a big enough deal to argue with her. The order of who is put over whom, with God as the head, is what's important.

# from 15175, 6550, 4691
--- When men abdicate
kicker: God's order in the home
big: Isaiah 3:12 | mark: children are their oppressors, and women rule over them
p: To the extent that women may usurp the authority of men, it is always the fault of men for abdicating their authority first. Adam, knowing the word of God, took the fruit and ate it to please Eve.
p: It's man's duty to God to love our women as Christ loves us. When we don't do our godly duty, society collapses. Men have been more traumatized and subverted than women. It's still up to us.
p: Far too many, male and female alike, stop reading at “submit” and take up the “war of the sexes” stances, bringing wrath and strife to what is a unifying principle of God.

# from 9271, 13605, 15662, 17509
--- Godly women used mightily
kicker: God's order in the home
big: Luke 8:2-3 | mark: which ministered unto him of their substance
p: Women in the word of God are not weak and incidental. Deborah sat beneath a palm tree, and her God given wisdom brought people to her, in the absence of men stepping up ([[Judges 4:4-9]]). Women who ministered with Christ provided from their substance and traveled with the disciples.
p: Yes, a qualified pastor must be a male, and women are to keep silence in the services ([[1 Timothy 2:11-14]]). But women are not subject to every man. They are subject to their father or their husband, in church to the pastor (just as the men are). Christian women are called to modesty and meekness ([[1 Timothy 2:9-10]]).
read: app:doctrine-family~15175 | Women rule over them: men abdicating authority
read: app:doctrine-family~9271 | Women who ministered with Christ
read: app:doctrine-family~12446 | Hair length and the order of heads

=== Husbands and wives
# from 4691, 6550
--- Wives submit, husbands love
kicker: Husbands and wives
big: Ephesians 5:24-25 | mark: Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church
p: Women are shown “submit” and taught to resent it. Men are shown it, and taught entitlement, and none look at the responsibility being the head entails.
p: Men are called to love their wife as their own flesh. Protecting and providing for them as Jesus has for us. When men shirk this responsibility, women see no profit in submission. And the two who become one flesh, under God, tear themselves asunder ([[1 Peter 3:7]]).

# from 17435, 1650
--- A virtuous woman
kicker: Husbands and wives
big: Proverbs 31:10-12 | mark: her price is far above rubies
p: She is trustworthy, diligent, rising early. A hard worker, who manages a household, starts small businesses, buys land, makes it fruitful. She helps the poor, is generous and hospitable. Her children learn her law and the fear of God at her feet.
p: She takes care of the house and has a side hustle, to the benefit of her household rather than some megacorp. It's not that women didn't work at all. They built up a reputation based on their own merits and labors. *A prudent wife is from the LORD* ([[Proverbs 19:14]]).

# from 17170, 11372, 12445
--- Drink from thine own cistern
kicker: Husbands and wives
big: Matthew 5:28 | mark: hath committed adultery with her already in his heart
p: Today, how many married men are taken in by pornography and internet catfishing schemes? *Can a man take fire in his bosom, and his clothes not be burned?* ([[Proverbs 6:25-27]]) Delight in the wife of thy youth.
p: Our nakedness is to be for our spouse. This would extend to pornography, strippers, and every other form of nudity ([[Leviticus 18:6]]). God's law of jealousy protected both: the husband from secret adultery, and the wife from an obsessive husband ([[Numbers 5:12-15]]).

# from 3753, 15888, 846
--- Better to marry than to burn
kicker: Husbands and wives
big: 1 Corinthians 7:2-3 | mark: let every man have his own wife; render unto the wife due benevolence
p: To withhold relations with our spouse for reason other than brief periods of fasting, agreed upon, is defrauding our spouse ([[1 Corinthians 7:5]]).
p: If you are living with or fornicating with your boyfriend or girlfriend, you should stop and get married. And by a man's fornication you don't just make the child, you make the woman a mother. He is now on the hook for providing for both.

# from 7157
--- Trust the Lord to bring your Rebekah
kicker: Husbands and wives
big: Genesis 24:27 | mark: I being in the way, the LORD led me
p: So many young men seek their Rebekah, and go where they should not, not trusting in the Lord to guide them. I am firmly convinced, with the longview of being an old head, of seeing God's angels bringing me where I needed to be.
p: Don't be discouraged. And young ladies seeking a spouse, live Godly with hospitality, grace and kindness, and the man for you will show himself.
read: app:doctrine-family~4691 | Wives submit, husbands love
read: app:doctrine-family~17435 | Who can find a virtuous woman
read: app:doctrine-family~7157 | Trust the Lord to bring your Rebekah

=== Divorce and remarriage
# from 5375, 6253
--- What God hath joined together
kicker: Divorce and remarriage
big: Matthew 19:6-8 | mark: What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder; from the beginning it was not so
p: Again we see the mistaken impression that the Pharisees were legalistic and strict, when in reality they sought loopholes from God's law, and Jesus teaches a stricter interpretation. Moses' compromise on divorce came from the failures and weaknesses of men, not God's intent.
p: (Full disclosure, I am divorced and remarried, to a widow. This makes me an adulterer. It doesn't matter the circumstances. It is this because Jesus says it is. But, thankfully we are forgiven in Jesus.)

# from 6253
--- How Satan uses divorce
kicker: Divorce and remarriage
big: Malachi 2:16 | mark: he hateth putting away
p: First he gets us to justify divorce. Then fornication and cohabitation become normalized, because if divorce is inevitable, what's the point of marriage? And if divorce harms children, why have them in the first place? And so birth control and abortion become the norm. And Satan keeps accusing.
p: Many spouses have one foot out the door, looking for any cause to confirm the distrust in their hearts sown by the wicked culture that we have.

# from 16727, 16728
--- Do the hard thing
kicker: Divorce and remarriage
big: Ezra 10:3 | mark: let us make a covenant with our God to put away all the wives
p: Ezra's mass divorce was a man's idea, not God's. These men could have been removed from office, having disqualified themselves, as Nehemiah did with the priest ([[Nehemiah 13:28]]). Two wrongs don't always make a right.
p: When faced with a hard choice because of our sins, wait on God's will. Do the hard things. Not latch on to man's compromise. It can be hard living with a spouse who doesn't treat you right. God says stick it out.
read: app:doctrine-family~6253 | Divorce, the hardness of hearts, and Satan's accusations
read: app:doctrine-family~16728 | Do the hard thing, not man's compromise

=== Honour thy father and mother
# from 5226, 17394, 12057
--- The first commandment with promise
kicker: Honour thy father and mother
big: Ephesians 6:2-3 | mark: Honour thy father and mother; which is the first commandment with promise
p: Modern teaching misses the point of this commandment, limiting it almost exclusively to children obeying their parents. Honor in the Bible often means paying a price, providing financial support ([[1 Timothy 5:17]]).
p: *But if any provide not for his own, and specially for those of his own house, he hath denied the faith, and is worse than an infidel* ([[1 Timothy 5:8]]). Take in your parents in their old age. Provide for them.

# from 12435, 17395, 5226
--- Corban
kicker: Honour thy father and mother
big: Mark 7:11-13 | mark: It is Corban; Making the word of God of none effect through your tradition
p: People used the Corban to get out of honoring, that is financially supporting, their parents in their later years. The letter of the law used to justify corruption.
p: The refusal of children to take care of their parents, consigning them to nursing homes and the state, came before working moms, daycare and divorce. God put in place a multi-generational family where each generation provides something to the unit, and stability to society.

# from 17396, 12056, 15035
--- Obedience modeled by the Son
kicker: Honour thy father and mother
big: Philippians 2:8 | mark: became obedient unto death
p: Jesus provided the example of a lifelong commitment to honoring the Father. Loving God with your whole heart begins with fearing your parents. The Rechabites obeyed even their father's own rules, and God blessed their line ([[Jeremiah 35:18-19]]).
p: At the judgment seat of Christ, no one's going to give you rewards for how big a victim you were. You won't receive crowns because of how unfairly your parents treated you. But you will be judged for how well you honored them.

# from 15194
--- The rebellious son
kicker: Honour thy father and mother
big: 2 Chronicles 24:2 | mark: all the days of Jehoiada the priest
p: How often do we see the children of a Christian man, kept in subjection, seeing a crack in their father's character (for all have fallen short), grow to resent him? In that resentment their own sinful desires find a justification, and they tear down the moral authority in their life.
p: And once that authority is removed from them, they sink further and further into sin ([[2 Chronicles 24:17-18]]). Many such cases.
read: app:doctrine-family~5226 | Honour thy father and mother means providing for them
read: app:doctrine-family~17395 | Honour thy parents, not the tradition of men
read: app:doctrine-family~15194 | Joash and the rebellious son

=== Raising children
# from 12921, 17922, 17158
--- Teach them diligently
kicker: Raising children
big: Deuteronomy 6:6-7 | mark: thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children
p: Even godly Christian parents can become lax, believing that sharing the gospel with them and bringing them to church is sufficient. Hoping Godliness will be passed on by osmosis from one church service a week.
p: *Our fathers have told us, what work thou didst in their days* ([[Psalms 44:1]]). Tell your children of God moving in your life, so that they may learn to trust Him in hard times. *We were Pharaoh's bondmen in Egypt; and the LORD brought us out* ([[Deuteronomy 6:21]]).

# from 17265, 17195, 10466, 17276
--- The rod of correction
kicker: Raising children
big: Proverbs 13:24 | mark: He that spareth his rod hateth his son
p: A scorner is that way because his father didn't love him enough to chasten him. A wise son listens because his father cared enough to apply the rod ([[Proverbs 22:15]]; [[Proverbs 23:13-14]]). The rod teaches them that chastisement comes from love, and they get a picture of God the Father through you ([[Hebrews 12:6-11]]).
p: When we discipline, it must be with sound judgment and mercy, longsuffering and with grace as God gave us. And mothers, do not undercut the discipline your husband gives out ([[Proverbs 29:15]]).

# from 14668, 4023, 17276
--- Provoke not your children to wrath
kicker: Raising children
big: Ephesians 6:4 | mark: provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of the Lord
p: Some Christian men think the only way to protect their children from the world is as a tyrant. Their fear shows their children a lack of faith, and it can drive them away from the Lord. Many parents create a barter system in place of love, forgiving but not forgetting. This builds within a child the seeds of a works-based relationship with God.
p: Honesty about sin and consequences, how it has affected you personally, can help soften the blow when children realize Mom and Dad aren't perfect. And the gospel lets them know there is One who is perfect.

# from 15195, 13946, 14667, 15041
--- You cannot carry their salvation
kicker: Raising children
big: Proverbs 22:6 | mark: Train up a child in the way he should go
p: It isn't a guarantee, but it certainly is a great inoculation against the snares most people get caught on. Godly father/wicked son, wicked father/Godly sons are found from Adam and Cain straight through the Old Testament ([[1 Samuel 8:1-3]]). We cannot exert our own righteousness and salvation onto our children.
p: Remove the high places in your heart, and you increase the odds that your children will do the same. Read your Bible, be patient and fair. Rule well. Every kid is different, but start with scripture.

# from 13889, 7308
--- An heritage of the LORD
kicker: Raising children
big: Psalms 127:3-5 | mark: children are an heritage of the LORD
p: God determines when a woman has a child or not. He opens the wombs and closes them ([[1 Samuel 1:27]]). Today the world uses chemicals to keep women sterile, and kills children as burdens instead of blessings.
p: God is our goalie. We are to become one flesh, husband and wife, trusting in Him to provide and prevent. We should be producing multitudes of Godly children. It is the main way we increase the Lord's blessing in the world, other than soul winning. (I've done my part, believe me.)

# from 13118, 15064, 15032
--- With all gravity
kicker: Raising children
big: 1 Timothy 3:4 | mark: having his children in subjection with all gravity
p: God has given married men a great and terrible responsibility. To be meek, longsuffering, merciful and just... and with all gravity, bringing your house into subjection. If you don't understand the choices that come from that, especially with rebellious children, read Deuteronomy 21:18-21 and consider what could lead a parent there ([[Deuteronomy 21:18-21]]).
p: *One that ruleth well his own house* is not a clause that allows rebellious children who don't like how their parents chastised them to exercise a veto on a ministry.
read: app:doctrine-family~12921 | Teach them diligently unto thy children
read: app:doctrine-family~10466 | Biblical parenting and the rod
read: app:doctrine-family~14668 | Provoke not your children to wrath
read: app:doctrine-family~7308 | Children are a blessing; trust God with the womb

=== Serve the LORD
--- As for Me and My House [title]
overline: Marriage, family & the home
heading: We Will Serve the LORD
big: Joshua 24:15 | mark: as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD
center: Obedient children are a reflection of Christ and good parents are a reflection of the Lord. Our behavior as parents is how children learn about God.
